"""Scientific report and claim ledger generated from immutable tables."""
from .core import *

def generate(write=True):
 read=lambda part,n:pd.read_csv(OUT/part/'tables'/f'{n}.csv');sa=read('part_a','endpoint_summary');ca=read('part_a','endpoint_counts');sb=read('part_b','endpoint_summary');cb=read('part_b','endpoint_counts');effects=read('part_b','factorial_intervals');conditional=read('part_b','conditional_paired');window=read('part_b','window_intervals');blocks=read('part_b','block_transfer');geo=read('part_b','geometry');end=read('part_b','endpoints');matha=read('part_a','mathematical_checks');mathb=read('part_b','mathematical_checks')
 def row(summary,arm,k,cue,metric='ce',subgroup='all'):return summary[(summary.arm==arm)&(summary['update']==k)&(summary.cue==cue)&(summary.metric==metric)&(summary.subgroup==subgroup)].iloc[0]
 def cnt(counts,arm,k,cue,subgroup='all'):return counts[(counts.arm==arm)&(counts['update']==k)&(counts.cue==cue)&(counts.subgroup==subgroup)].iloc[0]
 lines=['# Recurrent initialization, context centering and generalization','',
 'Both initial recurrent dynamics and initial context organization matter. Normalization improves familiar acquisition but does not guarantee C transfer: at330 the normalized independent arm has20/20 strong familiar learners but only9/20 C successes. Initially centering the same normalized draws gives20/20 familiar and C successes. With High recurrence, centering also helps C among competent learners, but full-strength Mixed can still fail. Thus C transfer and simultaneous full-strength cue combination are distinct outcomes.','',
 'HI=High/independent; HC=High/initially centered; NI=normalized/independent; NC=normalized/initially centered. Allfour arms use fully trainable direct A/B columns. PartA’s old permanently Centered architecture remains a separate cohort.','',
 '## Fixed comparison and fidelity','',
 'For each of20 paired seeds, the original native factory creates one canonical High draw (including default-module RNG consumption before Normal(0,2) redraw). Only Wh is scaled to spectral norm.9 for NI/NC; only the common initial context vector is removed for HC/NC: g=(WA+WB)/2,d=(WA−WB)/2, WA=d,WB=−d. Independent arms retain exact sampled columns without a floating-point g±d roundtrip. All other shared tensors, parameter registration, policy state, direct-wi Adam coordinates and optimizer initialization match. Initially centered g may learn immediately; it is not clamped.','',
 'The existing identity-activation8-unit LinearElman arithmetic, token4+cue3 input, four-class head and zero h0 are unchanged. Inputs[0,1,2,0,3,1,2], targets[1,2,0,3,1,2,3]; no position/history features. Source CE+.20 detached-confidence execution objective, two-parameter monotonic policy, Adam(.005 defaults), and joint clip1 are imported unchanged.330 A10/B10 updates use only A/B in the loss. Recurrent normalization occurs once; no protected-cue tuning, checkpoint selection, retries for performance or rescue training.','',
 'All80 complete trajectories and26,480 frozen model/policy/Adam states are retained. HI is **not independent** replication: its120 archived snapshots and100 corresponding update records are reused, with6,500 exact source updates reconstructing missing states. HC/NI/NC require19,800 new updates. Total new optimizer steps26,300; logical trajectory-update records26,400. HI actual pre-update losses match the historical source bitwise; available endpoint branches are reused. All models remained finite. An erroneous bitwise centered-identity assertion stopped after HI seed0; correcting it to the preregistered float bounds repeated no optimizer step. Both executed source versions and failing log remain archived.','',
 '## Part A: both Mixed encodings in existing models','',
 'Frozen evaluation precedes new training. Archived A/B/Mixed-average/C branches, certified zero-channel NoContext copies and permanent-g=0 Mixed-both copies supply72,820 cells;6,620 missing Standard Mixed-both rollouts supply the rest. No PartA optimizer is constructed.','',
 '| Existing arm | Update | Average CE | Both CE | C CE | Both success | Strong A/B |',
 '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for arm in ['Standard','Centered']:
  for k in [100,330]:
   n=int(cnt(ca,arm,k,'C','strong_familiar')['n']);lines.append(f'| {arm} | {k} | {row(sa,arm,k,"Mixed-average")["mean"]:.6f} | {row(sa,arm,k,"Mixed-both")["mean"]:.6f} | {row(sa,arm,k,"C")["mean"]:.6f} | {int(cnt(ca,arm,k,"Mixed-both").successes)}/20 | {n}/20 |')
 r=row(sa,'Standard',100,'C','delta_mixed');lines+=['',f'At100, Standard Both−Average CE={r["mean"]:.6f},95% seed CI[{r.ci_low:.6f},{r.ci_high:.6f}]. Average and C succeed20/20, Both19/20; among18 familiar-qualified networks, Both17/18. Permanent Centered Average=Both=C at every state, with all20 successful by100. The encoding change is therefore measurable in the existing Standard models, although most still succeed. These g/d-coordinate, differently drawn models are not matched factorial arms.','',
 '## Part B: acquisition and transfer','',
 'Strong familiar learning requires CE≤.5 and accuracy≥6/7 separately in both A/B. Per-cue success uses the same cutoffs. All20 seeds remain in primary means; familiar-qualified results are descriptive strata with explicit denominators.','',
 '| Arm | Update | Familiar CE | Average CE | Both CE | C CE | Strong A/B | Qualified C | Qualified Both |',
 '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for arm in ARMS:
  for k in [100,170,330]:
   n=int(cnt(cb,arm,k,'C','strong_familiar')['n']);cc=int(cnt(cb,arm,k,'C','strong_familiar').successes);bc=int(cnt(cb,arm,k,'Mixed-both','strong_familiar').successes)
   vals=[row(sb,arm,k,'C','familiar_ce')['mean'],*[row(sb,arm,k,c)['mean'] for c in ['Mixed-average','Mixed-both','C']]];lines.append(f'| {arm} | {k} | '+' | '.join(f'{v:.6f}' for v in vals)+f' | {n}/20 | {cc}/{n} | {bc}/{n} |')
 lines+=['', 'Zero-denominator entries establish no conditional effect. Updates80/120, all-six-cue accuracy, Both−Average and C−Both losses, chance comparisons, individual seeds and all subgroup intervals are supplied in each part’s endpoint tables. No denominator is chosen using protected performance.','',
 '| Arm at330 | C mean | C median | Both mean | Both median | C successes /20 | Both successes /20 |',
 '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for arm in ARMS:
  c=row(sb,arm,330,'C');bb=row(sb,arm,330,'Mixed-both');lines.append(f'| {arm} | {c["mean"]:.6f} | {c["median"]:.6f} | {bb["mean"]:.6f} | {bb["median"]:.6f} | {int(cnt(cb,arm,330,"C").successes)} | {int(cnt(cb,arm,330,"Mixed-both").successes)} |')
 lines+=['', 'The large HI/HC means retain extreme finite losses; medians and seed distributions are complementary, never replacements or winsorized estimates. At330, all14 qualified HI networks succeed under Average but only2 under C and Both. All12 qualified HC networks succeed under C; only8 under Both (four exceed chance). NI has all20 strong familiar,9 C successes and14 Both successes. NC has20 successes for allthese criteria. C is operationally NoContext, not an arbitrary angular novel cue.','',
 '## Matched factorial estimates','',
 'For each seed, normalization=[(NI−HI)+(NC−HC)]/2; centering=[(HC−HI)+(NC−NI)]/2; interaction=(NC−NI)−(HC−HI). Whole paired seeds, not positions or conditions independently, are bootstrapped10,000 times (RNG20260925). CIs are pointwise descriptive, not multiplicity-adjusted. Mean CE contrasts remain primary; seed-contrast medians and success-proportion contrasts are also retained.','',
 '| Update | C CE effect | Mean within-seed contrast | 95% CI |',
 '|---|---|---:|---|']
 for r in effects[(effects.metric=='C_ce')&effects['update'].isin([100,170,330])].itertuples():lines.append(f'| {r.update} | {r.effect} | {r.mean:.6f} | [{r.ci_low:.6f},{r.ci_high:.6f}] |')
 lines+=['', 'Negative normalization/centering contrasts mean lower C loss. Their positive interaction reflects nonadditivity on the raw CE scale, heavily influenced by High-independent extremes; it is not a neural interaction mechanism. The success counts do not support “only NC can transfer”: HC often transfers to C, especially when it learns A/B.','',
 'For the most comparable acquisition case, NI and NC both have20/20 strong familiar learners at330, with mean familiar CE≈.000224 versus.000265, yet markedly different C performance. The paired NC−NI C CE contrast is:']
 r=conditional[(conditional.comparison=='center_normalized')&(conditional['update']==330)&(conditional.subgroup=='both_strong')&(conditional.metric=='C_ce')].iloc[0];lines.append(f'{r["mean"]:.6f},CI[{r.ci_low:.6f},{r.ci_high:.6f}],n={int(r.n)} pairs.')
 lines+=['', 'This rules out failure to meet the familiar-acquisition criterion as the whole explanation in that comparison. It does not demonstrate mediation or strict independence from the acquisition trajectory. Other common-qualified strata are post-training descriptive subsets, not randomized conditional effects. Their actual330 sample sizes and C contrasts are:']
 for r in conditional[(conditional['update']==330)&(conditional.subgroup=='both_strong')&(conditional.metric=='C_ce')].itertuples():lines.append(f'- {r.comparison}:n={r.n},difference={r.mean:.6f},CI[{r.ci_low:.6f},{r.ci_high:.6f}].')
 lines+=['',
 '## Context dependence and learned computation','',
 'Same-weight switches use incoming−outgoing CE at states10..320;330 is end-censored. Complete10-update blocks give OwnGain=L_own(start)−L_own(end), CrossGain=L_other(start)−L_other(end), Specificity=OwnGain−CrossGain. Raw signs, baseline-adjusted costs and allindividual observations remain in CSVs. Positive specificity can coexist with transfer or interference; it is not an independent-skill criterion.','',
 '| Arm | Early A specificity [95%CI] | Early B specificity [95%CI] | Late floor blocks /460 | Hidden distance:initial→330 |',
 '|---|---|---|---:|---|']
 for arm in ARMS:
  rr=[]
  for cue in ['A','B']:
   x=window[(window.arm==arm)&(window.window=='early')&(window.practiced==cue)&(window.metric=='specificity')].iloc[0];rr.append(f'{x["mean"]:.4f}[{x.ci_low:.4f},{x.ci_high:.4f}]')
  n=blocks[(blocks.arm==arm)&(blocks.window=='late')].floor_at_start.sum();a=geo[(geo.arm==arm)&(geo['update']==0)].hidden_separation.mean();bb=geo[(geo.arm==arm)&(geo['update']==330)].hidden_separation.mean();lines.append(f'| {arm} | {rr[0]} | {rr[1]} | {n} | {a:.3f}→{bb:.3f} |')
 lines+=['', 'Early=blocks ending≤100; late=101..330. Floor flags mean both familiar losses≤.05 at block start, fixed before outcomes. NI/NC show positive early preferential learning in both directions while preserving transfer. High-arm early estimates are large and uncertain: HC both intervals include zero; HI only the B interval excludes zero. Nonzero initial/late geometry is not evidence that separate skills were learned. Late normalized blocks mostly begin at floor, so apparent weakening cannot establish shared learning. The earlier joint functional splitting criterion remains unchanged and **unassessed**; no restored-Adam diagnostics were added.','',
 'At a fixed checkpoint, baseline h0 is the token/bias trajectory. The cue response obeys U_t=Wh U_(t−1)+g,V_t=Wh V_(t−1)+d,starting at0; u_t=Wo U_t,v_t=Wo V_t. Thus zA=z0+u+v,zB=z0+u−v,zAverage=z0+u,zBoth=z0+2u,zC=z0. The cue response itself is independent of the particular identical token stream at fixed weights; its norm is not proof of reusable sequence knowledge.','',
 '| Arm at330 | ||g|| | Centered ||u|| | Centered ||v|| | Current ||Wh||₂ |',
 '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for arm in ARMS:
  gg=geo[(geo.arm==arm)&(geo['update']==330)].mean(numeric_only=True);lines.append(f'| {arm} | {gg.g_norm:.6f} | {gg.u_norm:.6f} | {gg.v_norm:.6f} | {gg.recurrent_spectral_norm:.6f} |')
 lines+=['', 'High recurrence can amplify a small learned g into a large common logit response: HC’s learned g is modest while its u can be large. NI retains a larger common input and common output response than NC. These associations, baseline C losses and margin changes are consistent with initialization biasing where accurate computation resides, but are not demonstrated causal mediation. g is free to regrow in HC/NC; neither has a permanent C guarantee. Native initial HC u may be slightly nonzero from float32 cancellation even though parameter g is exactly zero; the retained precision bounds distinguish this from learned common drive.','',
 '## Mathematical and implementation controls','',
 'At every position/state, Average=(A+B)/2 and Both=A+B−C in logits and hidden states; C=NoContext. Jensen guarantees CE_Average≤(CE_A+CE_B)/2 only. Both is an affine extrapolation relative to the trained A/B segment and has no such bound. Logit averaging does not average softmax probabilities, accuracy or CE; explicit counterexamples are tested. Even an average CE≤.5 does not itself guarantee accuracy≥6/7. Initially centered equality holds at0 up to numerical precision; permanent Centered equality holds throughout.','',
 f'All{len(matha)+len(mathb):,} position controls pass:fixed double tolerance1e−10+1e−12×scale, plus separate64eps absolute-summand bounds propagated through|Wh| for float32. Maximum double Both-logit residual={max(matha.double_both_logits_error.max(),mathb.double_both_logits_error.max()):.3g}; maximum native float32 Both residual={max(matha.float32_both_logits_error.max(),mathb.float32_both_logits_error.max()):.3g}. Large absolute roundoff at extreme High amplitudes is retained, not silently declared exact. CE allowances are twice the logit bounds. C/NoContext agree in all hidden/logit/probability entries; the permanent Centered three-way equality is exact in archived native outputs.','',
 '## Figures and exact evidence','',
 '- [FigureA:existing models, two Mixed encodings](part_a/figures/A_existing_mixed_encodings.png).',
 '- [Figure1:actual A10/B10 full/early loss](part_b/figures/01_training_loss.png); [scale companion](part_b/figures/01_training_loss_scale_companion.png). Produced before endpoint interpretation.',
 '- [Figure2:all six cue losses,full/early](part_b/figures/02_all_context_learning.png).',
 '- [Figure3:switches and raw own/cross learning](part_b/figures/03_switch_costs_and_transfer.png).',
 '- [Figure4:baseline,common/contrast responses,margin effects,dynamics](part_b/figures/04_learned_computation.png); [geometry/input-weight companion](part_b/figures/04_geometry_companion.png).',
 '- [Figure5:factorial endpoints,individual seeds and CIs](part_b/figures/05_factorial_endpoints.png).','',
 'SVG versions and exact CSV inputs/intervals accompany each PNG. PartA has79,440 six-cue evaluations and556,080 position rows; PartB158,880 evaluations and1,112,160 position rows. Full states, logits, probabilities, margins, z0/u/v, behavior, all means/medians/subgroup denominators, source/checkpoint SHA256s and seedwise factorial estimates are retained. claim_ledger.csv links claims to exact source hashes. Read-only verification and table-only byte-identical figure regeneration are documented in the code README.','',
 'The controlled evidence supports two roles: initial normalization helps acquisition and reduces extreme C loss, while initial removal of the common cue drive strongly improves C transfer, including when final familiar acquisition is comparable. Full-strength cue combination is a separate demand and can remain poor despite C success. Early context-specific learning can coexist with successful transfer in NC; persistent independent learning and a full human analogue remain unestablished.']
 text='\n'.join(lines)+'\n'
 if write:
  (OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text(text)
  claims=[('A1','Encoding changes existing Standard performance; permanent Centered identical','part_a/tables/endpoint_summary.csv'),('B1','Fixed full cohort, no outcome tuning','part_b/tables/training.csv'),('B2','Matched canonical initial draws and state provenance','part_b/tables/checkpoint_registry.csv'),('B3','HI historical reconstruction not independent replication','part_b/tables/historical_fidelity.csv'),('B4','Acquisition/generalization counts differ by initial factors','part_b/tables/endpoint_counts.csv'),('B5','Extreme means and medians both retained','part_b/tables/endpoint_summary.csv'),('B6','Within-seed factorial mean/success effects','part_b/tables/factorial_intervals.csv'),('B7','Common-familiar comparisons descriptive with actual n','part_b/tables/conditional_paired.csv'),('B8','Signed context-specific learning and floor limitation','part_b/tables/window_intervals.csv'),('B9','Current learned g/d/dynamics and geometry','part_b/tables/geometry.csv'),('B10','Label-scored margins and full z0/u/v contributions','part_b/tables/decomposition.csv'),('M1','Avg Jensen only; both affine identity; CNoContext','part_b/tables/mathematical_checks.csv'),('M2','Permanent centered identity and source reuse','part_a/tables/mathematical_checks.csv')]
  pd.DataFrame([dict(claim_id=i,claim=c,source=n,sha256=sha(OUT/n),limitation='Descriptive functional/representation measures; original splitting gate unassessed' if i in ['B8','B9','B10'] else 'C=NoContext; no mediation claim; seed unit20') for i,c,n in claims]).to_csv(OUT/'claim_ledger.csv',index=False)
  (OUT/'RESEARCHER_HANDOFF.md').write_text('''# Researcher teach-back

The two factors are initial Wh normalization and removal of the initial shared cue component g. Allfour arms have directly trainable A/B columns; HC/NC can regrow g. C supplies no input because its third channel is zero, so this is specifically sequence prediction without familiar cue drive.

At fixed weights, zAverage=z0+u and zBoth=z0+2u, while zC=z0. Only Average is Jensen-bounded by familiar A/B CE. Doubling the common cue response can help or hurt different classes/positions; it is not probability pooling. A large response norm is not causal evidence for its behavioral effect.

At330, NI and NC both have20/20 strong familiar learners, but C succeeds9/20 versus20/20. HI has14 familiar learners and2 qualified C successes. HC has12 familiar learners,all12 C successes,but only8 full-strength Mixed successes. Initialization centering therefore helps transfer; normalization alone is insufficient. Familiar-qualified and common-qualified strata are descriptive,not causal mediation. The common-success design does not establish a general retrieval policy.

Early normalized learning is context-specific with cross-context transfer; late floor-limited loss changes cannot establish shared or persistent independent learning. Geometry was already nonzero at initialization and remains separated. Original functional-splitting gate unchanged/unassessed.

Read REPORT.md and primary Figures1/2 first. part_a/ and part_b/ remain distinct. Tables retain actual practiced losses,frozen six-cue results,full position logits/probabilities/hidden states,raw signed gains/switches,centered z0/u/v vectors,margins,g/d,current Wh norms and seedwise factorial contrasts. checkpoint_registry.csv hashes80 all-state bundles; source_reuse_registry.csv hashes120 original HI snapshots. HI is exact historical reconstruction,not20 independent new replications.100 saved update records reused;26,300 new steps (19,800 new plus6,500 missing-state reconstruction).No training repeated after the retained validation correction.

Use experiments.recurrent_context_factorial.verify for read-only checks and --regenerate with a new empty folder for all16 figure files. Never rerun training modules. The final seal covers code,source mappings,test logs,scratchpad and scientific evidence. Csuccess does not establish angularNovel transfer; no new data/model/threshold search is warranted by these files.
''')
 return text
if __name__=='__main__':generate()
